s/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:35:25-07:00","id":1096900,"title":"","content":"Nareau is apparently the name of a spider creator-god of the Kiribati peoples of Micronesia. Marawa is a (possible trickster?) spider god from the Vanuatu peoples of Melanesia, apparently responsible for the fact that people die. Rati is the name of a Hindu goddess of lust, carnal desire and sexual pleasure. I'm not able to find any connection between her and spiders. <br /> <br /> I think they're meant to be the slightly twisted Kumo counterparts to the normal Hatar's Agere, Anomia, and Malum cabals. Rati, a facet of the Beast of War, as the Myrmidon; Nareau, a facet of the Eater of Souls, as the Viskr; and Marawa, a facet of the Defiler Wyrm, as the Wyrsta. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:42:20-07:00","id":1096903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1095744-marawa-nareau-and-rati?p=1096900#post1096900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nareau is apparently the name of a spider creator-god of the Kiribati peoples of Micronesia. Marawa is a (possible trickster?) spider god from the Vanuatu peoples of Melanesia, apparently responsible for the fact that people die. Rati is the name of a Hindu goddess of lust, carnal desire and sexual pleasure. I'm not able to find any connection between her and spiders.<br /> <br /> I think they're meant to be the slightly twisted Kumo counterparts to the normal Hatar's Agere, Anomia, and Malum cabals. Rati, a facet of the Beast of War, as the Myrmidon; Nareau, a facet of the Eater of Souls, as the Viskr; and Marawa, a facet of the Defiler Wyrm, as the Wyrsta. .</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that they don't act a thing like the Triatic manifestations that you might expect. Rati is very much the opposite of a murder-happy berserker, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:24:57-07:00","id":1096912,"title":"","content":"Blood-lust, maybe? No idea what the thought process behind picking the names was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T18:33:16-07:00","id":1096941,"title":"","content":"I'm going to guess they are each a Wyrmish being with a sub attachment to another member of the triat. Like maybe Rati is Wyrm/Wyrm from the Rathi warriors in Vedic lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:26:20-07:00","id":1096966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1095744-marawa-nareau-and-rati?p=1096941#post1096941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to guess they are each a Wyrmish being with a sub attachment to another member of the triat. Like maybe Rati is Wyrm/Wyrm from the Rathi warriors in Vedic lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for extra complication points, they allocated things through Daoism instead, so you have Rati as Yang, and the other two as Yin and Balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:45:07-08:00","id":1179080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1095744-marawa-nareau-and-rati?p=1096900#post1096900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're meant to be the slightly twisted Kumo counterparts to the normal Hatar's Agere, Anomia, and Malum cabals. Rati, a facet of the Beast of War, as the Myrmidon; Nareau, a facet of the Eater of Souls, as the Viskr; and Marawa, a facet of the Defiler Wyrm, as the Wyrsta. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you're drawing the Triatic Wyrm associations based on their Yin/Yang associations relative to the broader Triat. That is to say, you're associating Marawa with the Defiler Wyrm because he's associated with Yin, as is the Wyrm; and Rati you're associating with the Beast of War because she's associated with Yang like the Wyld is.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest however that as the Hengeyokai interpret the Triat differently than Western Fera do, so to must the Triatic Wyrm be interpreted differently.<br /> <br /> The Western perspective is that in a healthy state, the Triat has Chaos (Wyld) and Order (Weaver) at odds with the force of Destruction (Wyrm) keeping the balance.<br /> <br /> The Eastern perspective appears to be Creation/Yang (Wyld) set against Destruction/Yin (Wyrm) with Preservance (Weaver) keeping the balance.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, the Beast of War, while seen as reflecting Chaos in the West, is the pure Destroyer reflecting itself in the Eastern view (fitting Marawa), while the perverse passions of the Defiler Wyrm reflect the raw fecundity of the Wyld (fitting Rati).<br /> <br /> PS: sorry for the necro, but I was reading up on this topic and responding here seemed better than starting a new thread on my interpretation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:13:42-08:00","id":1179223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1095744-marawa-nareau-and-rati?p=1179080#post1179080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume you're drawing the Triatic Wyrm associations based on their Yin/Yang associations relative to the broader Triat. That is to say, you're associating Marawa with the Defiler Wyrm because he's associated with Yin, as is the Wyrm; and Rati you're associating with the Beast of War because she's associated with Yang like the Wyld is.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest however that as the Hengeyokai interpret the Triat differently than Western Fera do, so to must the Triatic Wyrm be interpreted differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it really seems to be a kind of cosmic constant. Not that there's much information about it in comparison to the spotlight that gets put on the Yama Kings, which have another division of Yin and Yang, which mostly revolves around whether or not they're attuned to the living or Dark Umbrae, as they're KotE antagonists and that's how it rolls with presenting the undeath of the devil-corpses. It breaks down a bit in other contexts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Western perspective is that in a healthy state, the Triat has Chaos (Wyld) and Order (Weaver) at odds with the force of Destruction (Wyrm) keeping the balance.<br /> <br /> The Eastern perspective appears to be Creation/Yang (Wyld) set against Destruction/Yin (Wyrm) with Preservance (Weaver) keeping the balance. </div> </div> </div>Except it really isn't, because they don't go into things like that. Also, the attempts to link in Daoist thought were not really very well integrated, particularly since Yin is not destruction so much as it is being passive, defensive, cold, heavy, and a number of other traits that you can read over in various places. Each of the Triat could exist in a spectrum between Shade and Bright. Also, when this perspective was first couched in the original writeup of the Kitsune in Caerns: Places of Power, the Wyrm was the Balance between Yin and Yang. The Triat itself is more often couched in terms of the Three Sacred Treasures of TCM, as noted on page 27 of Hengeyokai, though this is also not something that's given much consideration beyond the sidebar in which it appears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, with that in mind, the Beast of War, while seen as reflecting Chaos in the West, is the pure Destroyer reflecting itself in the Eastern view (fitting Marawa), while the perverse passions of the Defiler Wyrm reflect the raw fecundity of the Wyld (fitting Rati). </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, it could simply be idiosyncratic to the Kumo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PS: sorry for the necro, but I was reading up on this topic and responding here seemed better than starting a new thread on my interpretation </div> </div> </div>We haven't really gotten anything new on the subject in the books, though, and it's looking like we might not ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:27:23-08:00","id":1179477,"title":"","content":"So my problem with their being a sexy one is that i imagine all werespiders to be sexy, regardless of who they follow. It's the legs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\